WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.560
When a Jewish parent dies, their
children say a prayer called Kaddish.

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.440
They say it for eleven months, not twelve.

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.550
Why stop one month short?

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.320
Yet the early books of the Hebrew
Bible say little about heaven.

5
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.410
Their focus is this life.

6
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.110
So where did Jewish hope of
life after death come from?

7
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.020
In this mission, you'll meet Jewish
teaching on judgement after death,

8
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.830
on Gan Eden and on Gehinnom.

9
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.040
Then you'll weigh up whether these
beliefs still matter for Jews today.

10
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:34.590
Your mission: find out where Jewish
hope of life after death came from.
